---
import Base from '../../../layouts/Ui.astro';
---

<Base title="Buttons">
  <h1>Buttons &amp; badges</h1>
  <p>
    A button is a struck typewriter key: a plate in a 2px ink rule with the
    hard letterpress offset. Pressing it drives the plate into its own shadow
    — the one smooth motion in the language, 90ms and mechanical. Badges are
    ticket stubs.
  </p>

  <section class="mk-card">
    <h2>THE PLATES</h2>
    <p>
      The default plate, solid-ink primary, the ghost nav-link key, the STOP
      red, and the ochre warning plate. The warning plate spends the
      view&rsquo;s one accent ration — a page with an ochre button has no
      other ochre spot.
    </p>
    <div class="row">
      <button class="mk-btn mk-btn--primary">Print the bill</button>
      <button class="mk-btn">Hold for notes</button>
      <button class="mk-btn mk-btn--ghost">See the programme</button>
      <button class="mk-btn mk-btn--warning">Mind the sawdust</button>
      <button class="mk-btn mk-btn--danger">Strike the set</button>
    </div>
    <pre><code>&lt;button class="mk-btn mk-btn--primary"&gt;Print the bill&lt;/button&gt;
&lt;button class="mk-btn"&gt;Hold for notes&lt;/button&gt;
&lt;button class="mk-btn mk-btn--ghost"&gt;See the programme&lt;/button&gt;
&lt;button class="mk-btn mk-btn--warning"&gt;Mind the sawdust&lt;/button&gt;
&lt;button class="mk-btn mk-btn--danger"&gt;Strike the set&lt;/button&gt;</code></pre>
  </section>

  <section class="mk-card">
    <h2>SIZES</h2>
    <p>
      Tracking tightens as the plate shrinks; the face never swaps. The xs
      key is for pointer-dense ledgers — it sits below the 44px touch floor,
      so prefer sm on touch-first surfaces or give the row itself the tap
      target.
    </p>
    <div class="row" style="align-items: center;">
      <button class="mk-btn mk-btn--xs">Cut</button>
      <button class="mk-btn mk-btn--sm">Hold</button>
      <button class="mk-btn">Print</button>
      <button class="mk-btn mk-btn--lg">Curtain up</button>
    </div>
    <pre><code>&lt;button class="mk-btn mk-btn--xs"&gt;Cut&lt;/button&gt;
&lt;button class="mk-btn mk-btn--sm"&gt;Hold&lt;/button&gt;
&lt;button class="mk-btn"&gt;Print&lt;/button&gt;
&lt;button class="mk-btn mk-btn--lg"&gt;Curtain up&lt;/button&gt;</code></pre>
  </section>

  <section class="mk-card">
    <h2>HELD DOWN</h2>
    <p>
      <code>--active</code> is an honest selected state for segmented choices
      and nav keys: the pressed geometry becomes the resting state — the key
      is held down. Pair it with <code>aria-pressed</code> or
      <code>aria-current</code>.
    </p>
    <div class="row">
      <button class="mk-btn mk-btn--active" aria-pressed="true">Evening</button>
      <button class="mk-btn" aria-pressed="false">Matinee</button>
      <button class="mk-btn" aria-pressed="false">Midnight</button>
    </div>
    <pre><code>&lt;button class="mk-btn mk-btn--active" aria-pressed="true"&gt;Evening&lt;/button&gt;
&lt;button class="mk-btn" aria-pressed="false"&gt;Matinee&lt;/button&gt;</code></pre>
  </section>

  <section class="mk-card">
    <h2>SOLD OUT</h2>
    <p>
      Disabled empties the plate: faded text, tan rule, no shadow, no press.
      Nothing is greyed with opacity — the house simply prints
      &ldquo;sold out&rdquo; across the ticket window.
    </p>
    <div class="row">
      <button class="mk-btn mk-btn--primary" disabled>Sold out</button>
      <button class="mk-btn" disabled>Sold out</button>
      <button class="mk-btn mk-btn--ghost" disabled>Sold out</button>
      <button class="mk-btn mk-btn--danger" disabled>Sold out</button>
    </div>
    <pre><code>&lt;button class="mk-btn mk-btn--primary" disabled&gt;Sold out&lt;/button&gt;</code></pre>
  </section>

  <section class="mk-card">
    <h2>THE FULL MEASURE</h2>
    <p><code>--block</code> runs the key the full width of the column — narrow forms, phone sheets.</p>
    <div style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: var(--mk-space-sm); max-width: 22rem;">
      <button class="mk-btn mk-btn--primary mk-btn--block">Book the act</button>
      <button class="mk-btn mk-btn--block">Ask the neighbour first</button>
    </div>
    <pre><code>&lt;button class="mk-btn mk-btn--primary mk-btn--block"&gt;Book the act&lt;/button&gt;</code></pre>
  </section>

  <section class="mk-card">
    <h2>SINGLE-GLYPH KEYS</h2>
    <p>
      A square 44&times;44 plate for one glyph. House doctrine: there is no
      line-icon set — Unicode glyphs stand in the icon position. Always give
      the key an <code>aria-label</code>.
    </p>
    <div class="row">
      <button class="mk-btn mk-btn--icon" aria-label="Previous act">&larr;</button>
      <button class="mk-btn mk-btn--primary mk-btn--icon" aria-label="Add to the bill">+</button>
      <button class="mk-btn mk-btn--danger mk-btn--icon" aria-label="Strike from the bill">&times;</button>
      <button class="mk-btn mk-btn--icon" aria-label="Next act" disabled>&rarr;</button>
    </div>
    <pre><code>&lt;button class="mk-btn mk-btn--icon" aria-label="Previous act"&gt;&amp;larr;&lt;/button&gt;
&lt;button class="mk-btn mk-btn--primary mk-btn--icon" aria-label="Add to the bill"&gt;+&lt;/button&gt;</code></pre>
  </section>

  <section class="mk-card">
    <h2>TICKET STUBS</h2>
    <p>
      Badges are printed stubs: typewriter caps in a 1px rule. Success prints
      solid ink — a thing done needs no colour. Accent and warning share the
      ochre ration; add <code>--dot</code> for a leading printed square.
    </p>
    <div class="row">
      <span class="mk-badge">on the bill</span>
      <span class="mk-badge mk-badge--accent">held over</span>
      <span class="mk-badge mk-badge--success">performed</span>
      <span class="mk-badge mk-badge--warning">one night only</span>
      <span class="mk-badge mk-badge--danger">cancelled</span>
    </div>
    <div class="row">
      <span class="mk-badge mk-badge--dot mk-badge--success">now playing</span>
      <span class="mk-badge mk-badge--dot mk-badge--warning">intermission</span>
      <span class="mk-badge mk-badge--dot mk-badge--danger">dark tonight</span>
      <span class="mk-badge mk-badge--dot">unbilled</span>
    </div>
    <div class="row" style="align-items: center;">
      <span class="mk-badge mk-badge--sm">sm</span>
      <span class="mk-badge">default</span>
      <span class="note">— sm tightens the stub for dense ledger rows; the type stays legible</span>
    </div>
    <pre><code>&lt;span class="mk-badge mk-badge--success"&gt;performed&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="mk-badge mk-badge--dot mk-badge--danger"&gt;dark tonight&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="mk-badge mk-badge--sm"&gt;dense&lt;/span&gt;</code></pre>
  </section>

  <style>
    .row {
      display: flex;
      flex-wrap: wrap;
      gap: var(--mk-space-sm);
    }

    .row + .row {
      margin-top: var(--mk-space-sm);
    }

    .note {
      font-family: var(--mk-font-typewriter);
      font-size: var(--mk-size-mono-xs);
      letter-spacing: 0.06em;
      color: var(--mk-color-text-muted);
    }

    section.mk-card + section.mk-card {
      margin-top: var(--mk-space-2xl);
    }

    pre {
      margin-top: var(--mk-space-md);
      padding: 12px 14px;
      background: var(--mk-color-plate);
      border: var(--mk-rule-hair);
      border-left: var(--mk-rule-thick);
      color: var(--mk-color-heading);
      font-family: var(--mk-font-typewriter);
      font-size: var(--mk-size-mono-sm);
      line-height: 1.6;
      overflow-x: auto;
    }

    code {
      font-family: var(--mk-font-typewriter);
      font-size: 0.86em;
      background: var(--mk-color-plate);
      border: var(--mk-rule-hair);
      color: var(--mk-color-heading);
      padding: 1px 5px 0;
    }

    pre code {
      background: none;
      border: 0;
      padding: 0;
      font-size: inherit;
    }
  </style>
</Base>
